{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfZtS3ArNifiC2qAc8NcR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the exploratory candidate `pattern_coverage_detection`, and the admission self-check (`check_candidate`) printed `OK`.\n\n**Hypothesis:** people judge randomness by spotting patterns. They scan a sequence for streaks of identical flips and for stretches of strict H/T alternation, and a sequence looks less random the more of its flips fall inside a pattern long enough to notice. Everyone notices a streak at the same length, but the length at which an alternating stretch starts to look like a pattern differs from person to person. What drives the choice is how much of the sequence those patterns cover, not the overall switch rate. That is a different kind of process from the current set, which is built mostly on how close the alternation rate is to an ideal. It goes straight at the critique's one finding that survived the FDR correction: among pairs with similar alternation rates, people avoid long streaks more than the incumbent predicts.\n\n**Model:** for each sequence, the hook computes the share of flips inside runs of each length (2–8) and inside alternating stretches of each length (3–8). A smooth threshold on stretch length decides how strongly each length counts as a detected pattern. There are five parameters: how sharp that threshold is, the shared streak threshold, a personal alternation threshold per participant (non-centred hierarchical), and one sensitivity. The choice is a logistic function of the difference in pattern coverage between the two sequences.\n\n**Check results:**\n- **Admission check:** the model loads, its log-probability is finite and it meets the data contract.\n- **Smoke fit:** ELPD-LOO came out at −1127.3. That is 1 chain of 100 draws, so it isn't comparable to the incumbent's −973.3 from a full fit.\n- **Warnings:** PSIS-LOO was unreliable on the smoke fit (2.4% of trials had high Pareto k, above the 1% tolerance). Convergence wasn't verified, because one chain can't report R-hat.\n\nNovelty against the existing models and convergence under the full fit are still only tested at admission.\n\nThe three files are in `iter_3/candidate_2/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3635,"cache_read_input_tokens":62003,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3635,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4252804f-9998-4b79-a22d-729ed9aa0617","uuid":"031f0f97-fa93-4cde-bb83-be0198f052a6","timestamp":"2026-09-30T15:49:06.097Z","request_id":"req_011CfZtS2hq4E9DnvKnr46Gm"}
